    {
        "content": "<p>Today I was running vkmark on downstream tyr comparing it to panthor, and I have a new performance optimized config for v7.3-rc3 to share. <br>\n<a href=\"/user_uploads/35136/ZXejGOf8oW-mOk_4waqsqEJd/config.tyr.perf.v7.3-rc3\">config.tyr.perf.v7.3-rc3</a></p>",
        "id": 626163559,
        "sender_full_name": "Deborah Brouwer",
        "timestamp": 1790114165
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I started from the GFXBench config <code>config.tyr.performance</code> and then made these changes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>enable DRM_PANTHOR as a module</li>\n<li>default CPUFreq governor to performance</li>\n<li>enable devfreq performance governor</li>\n<li>disable ftrace</li>\n<li>disable PM debugging</li>\n<li>disable NFS and SUNRPC debugging</li>\n<li>enable CONFIG_SCHED_CLUSTER</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 626163738,
        "sender_full_name": "Deborah Brouwer",
        "timestamp": 1790114217
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"878151\">@Beata Michalska</span> I ran CTS tests on the the latest downstream branch from <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"532207\">@Sami Tolvanen</span>  <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/panfrost/linux/-/tree/sami/tyr/7.4/dev\">https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/panfrost/linux/-/tree/sami/tyr/7.4/dev</a> and the results are identical for tyr and panthor:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th><strong>Tyr — Nov 9</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Panthor — Nov 9</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Kernel base</td>\n<td><code>6628e7d4c6b2</code> (Linux 7.4-rc1)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mesa</td>\n<td>26.2.6</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vulkan CTS</td>\n<td>1.4.6.1</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Panthor uAPI</td>\n<td>v1.8</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pass</strong></td>\n<td><strong>268,649</strong></td>\n<td><strong>268,649</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fail</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Crash</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Skip</td>\n<td>813,864</td>\n<td>813,864</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Timeout</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flake</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ExpectedFail</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Warn</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total Tests</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1,082,520</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1,082,520</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CI Links</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115536096\">Job 1</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115536097\">Job 2</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115536098\">Job 3</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115536099\">Job 4</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115555978\">Job 1</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115555979\">Job 2</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115555980\">Job 3</a> · <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/dbrouwer/mesa/-/jobs/115555981\">Job 4</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>i also ran vkmark <a href=\"https://github.com/vkmark/vkmark\">https://github.com/vkmark/vkmark</a> and the two drivers are also performing roughly the same:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th><strong>Configuration</strong></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>Tyr FPS</strong></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>Tyr FrameTime (ms)</strong></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>Panthor FPS</strong></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>Panthor FrameTime (ms)</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Kernel base</strong></td>\n<td><code>6628e7d4c6b2</code> (Linux 7.4-rc1)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mesa</strong></td>\n<td>26.2.6</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Benchmark</strong></td>\n<td>vkmark 2025.01</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>vertex</td>\n<td>device-local=true</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4661</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.215</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4683</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.214</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>vertex</td>\n<td>device-local=false</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4718</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.212</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4683</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.214</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>texture</td>\n<td>anisotropy=0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5335</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.187</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5177</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.193</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>texture</td>\n<td>anisotropy=16</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5314</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.188</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5160</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.194</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>shading</td>\n<td>shading=gouraud</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4053</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.247</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4008</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>shading</td>\n<td>shading=blinn-phong-inf</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4027</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.248</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3986</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.251</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>shading</td>\n<td>shading=phong</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3501</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.286</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3428</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.292</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>shading</td>\n<td>shading=cel</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3431</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.291</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">3391</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.295</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>effect2d</td>\n<td>kernel=edge</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4103</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.244</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">4052</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.247</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>effect2d</td>\n<td>kernel=blur</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1647</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.607</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1642</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.609</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>desktop</td>\n<td>default</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5636</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.177</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5505</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.182</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>cube</td>\n<td>default</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">7244</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.138</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">7092</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.141</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>clear</td>\n<td>default</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">6029</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.166</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">5938</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0.168</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>vkmark Score</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>4592</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>4518</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
        "id": 638895753,
        "sender_full_name": "Deborah Brouwer",
        "timestamp": 1794266717
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you Deborah .<br>\nThey are very close indeed.<br>\nHas anyone tried to get some power metrics?</p>",
        "id": 639054038,
        "sender_full_name": "Beata Michalska",
        "timestamp": 1794293780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I haven't at least. Do you  a specific test in mind?</p>",
        "id": 639275571,
        "sender_full_name": "Deborah Brouwer",
        "timestamp": 1794344049
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just out of curiosity at this point.</p>",
        "id": 639539109,
        "sender_full_name": "Beata Michalska",
        "timestamp": 1794419798
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"532207\">@Sami Tolvanen</span>  : would you be able to share your results as well here ?</p>",
        "id": 639768920,
        "sender_full_name": "Beata Michalska",
        "timestamp": 1794493222
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I re-ran GFXBench on my board with the current tyr-dev and while the Vulkan benchmarks are on par with Panthor, I noticed that GL benchmarks are lagging behind currently. I'm not entirely surprised since nobody has looked into optimizing this branch yet.</p>\n<p>I uploaded <a href=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/samitolvanen/linux/-/tree/sami/tyr/7.4/fixes?ref_type=heads\">some fixes and optimizations</a> that I've been working on recently and they seem to fix the GL benchmark issue. Here's a comparison:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Benchmark</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Panthor</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">tyr-dev</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">sami/tyr/7.4/fixes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">vulkan_5_normal_off</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">28.83 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">28.83 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">28.83 FPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">vulkan_5_normal</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">57.60 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">57.60 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">57.61 FPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">gl_5_normal</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">54.34 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">49.83 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">59.53 FPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">gl_manhattan31_off</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">35.08 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">31.85 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">39.32 FPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">gl_manhattan31</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">57.29 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">52.30 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">60.02 FPS (vsync cap)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">gl_trex_off</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">103.22 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">102.01 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">108.56 FPS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">gl_trex</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">62.21 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">62.20 FPS</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">62.17 FPS (vsync cap)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Note that the plan is to switch to a different JobQueue implementation once it's upstream, so we'll have to re-test after that.</p>\n<p>What comes to power consumption, I don't believe Rock 5B provices a convenient way to measure that. We have power measurements from a different device with an ODPM, but this is on AM hardware/driver, so the numbers are not relevant for upstream Tyr.</p>",
        "id": 639878351,
        "sender_full_name": "Sami Tolvanen",
        "timestamp": 1794514492
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi Sami, thank you for the numbers. I yet have to see what changes you have had to make to restore the performance for GL tests. It would also be interesting to see how the new job queue will be performing</p>",
        "id": 640108208,
        "sender_full_name": "Beata Michalska",
        "timestamp": 1794581596
    }
]